quran[11]{c,v,t}:
  39,57,"Or one should say: ‘If only Allah had guided me, I would have surely been among the God-conscious.’"
  39,58,"Or one should say when he sees the punishment: ‘If only there had been a second chance for me, I would be among the virtuous.’"
  39,59,"(Allah will say:) ‘Nay! My revelations did come to you, but you denied them and acted arrogantly, and you were among the disbelievers.’"
  39,60,"On the Day of Resurrection, you will see those who attributed lies to Allah having their faces blackened. Is not the final abode of the arrogant in Hell?"
  39,61,"Allah will deliver those who were God-conscious, bestowing (them) with (ultimate) success. No evil will touch them, nor will they grieve."
  39,62,Allah is the Creator of everything. And He is the Guardian over everything.
  39,63,"To Him belong the keys (to the treasures) of the heavens and the earth. And those who disbelieve in the revelations of Allah, it is they who are the losers."
  39,64,"Say: ‘Are you urging me to worship (someone) other than Allah, O you senseless people!’"
  39,65,"Indeed, it has been revealed to you and those before you: ‘(O people!) If you ascribe partners (to Allah), your deeds will certainly be void, and you shall surely be among the losers."
  39,66,"Rather, worship Allah (alone) and be among the grateful.’"
  39,67,"They do not appreciate Allah’s Glory with the appreciation that is due to Him. Yet the entire earth will be in His Grip on the Day of Resurrection, and the heavens will be rolled up in His right Hand. Glory be to Him (and) Exalted is He above whatever they associate (with Him)."
